course: dictionary
lesson: 15461
title: A word for a must
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A stipulation is a rule or condition that must be kept, like the small print on a deal. Formal writers use it when something is a must. Look at «The library lends the book, with the stipulation that you return it on time.» The word «with the stipulation that» tells you a rule comes next, and the rule is: return it on time.
explain: The clue words are the important part. Look for «as long as», «on condition that», or «provided that». These all mean the same thing as a stipulation: something must happen first. «You may join the club, as long as you are ten or older.» Being ten or older is the stipulation.
explain: The verb stipulate means to state clearly that something must happen. «The rules stipulate that every player must wear a helmet.» The rules say clearly that wearing a helmet is a must. In maths word problems, a stipulation is a condition the answer must meet, so check your answer against every stipulation.
fact: A stipulation is a condition or rule that must be kept as part of an agreement.
fact: «Stipulation» is a formal word, used in contracts, rules and competitions.
fact: Plain words for stipulation are condition, rule, and «as long as».
fact: «Stipulate» is the verb: to state clearly that something must happen.
fact: In a maths problem, a stipulation is a condition the answer must meet, such as «each group has the same number».
exercise: «The library lends the book, with the stipulation that you return it on time.» What does stipulation mean here? | A short story inside the book | A kind of library card | A picture on the front cover | *A rule or condition that must be kept
exercise: «The rules stipulate that every player must wear a helmet.» What does stipulate mean? | To ask a question politely | To lose the game | *To state clearly that something must happen | To dance around the pitch
exercise: Share 20 pencils into boxes, with the stipulation that each box holds the same number. What is the stipulation? | The colour of the pencils | *Each box must hold the same number | The number of boxes must be ten | The total number of pencils
test: «You may join the club, as long as you are ten or older.» Which words show the stipulation? | Join the club | You may | The club | *as long as you are ten or older
test: «The shop will sell the bike, on condition that you show a receipt.» What is the stipulation? | The bike is red | *You must show a receipt | You may keep the bike forever | The shop is closed
exam: «The contest has one stipulation: every entry must be original.» Which word means a rule that must be kept? | contest | entry | *stipulation | original
